I went through grueling budget hearings grueling budget hearings my first term on the council ruling budget hearings and I think what I'm going to ask is for the city clerk to pull up all of the budget questions that were asked in the 2015 budget year 2016 budget years in the 2017 budget year 2016, I'd like to see those yes, I'd like to see.

1423
02:02:47,040 --> 02:02:53,404
take a look just to see just to see what the dynamic was at that point in time, and what that counselor was asking for.

1424
02:02:54,144 --> 02:02:57,346
And then maybe we can ask the question what happened when you went across the hall.

1425
02:02:58,426 --> 02:03:03,329
And I do want to make clear this is not my desire to do this I don't think it's anyone's desire to do this.

1426
02:03:03,529 --> 02:03:06,371
Yeah, and I've been asking.

1427
02:03:06,591 --> 02:03:09,953
And I've been asking for a budget, you know, since the very beginning of the year.

1428
02:03:10,573 --> 02:03:15,018
And just again to make clear to people listening in, we're doing it this way because we have no choice.

1429
02:03:15,378 --> 02:03:32,256
We're up against deadline we can meet now and have partial information, or we can meet as proposed by the administration on the 28th with, you know, even less information, two days, and I just want to make that extremely clear so that when this council has to vote on something we've been backed into a corner.

1430
02:03:33,258 --> 02:03:39,183
we, you know, by time, by, by state statute, this is not at all how any of us want to do this process.

1431
02:03:39,363 --> 02:03:40,364
And I just want to make that clear.

1432
02:03:40,984 --> 02:04:01,881
And I just want to add after councilor has put information and we'll take a point of information from the president, my attempt to reach a cordial and what at this point within the constraints that we have of the timeline, reasonable approach to get the documents does not mean that I'm not unhappy with the way that this process has worked out unhappy with the timeline.

1433
02:04:03,150 --> 02:04:08,811
more frustrated now even than before to hear that the idea of coming with the budget on the 28th when the deadline is the 30th.

1434
02:04:09,092 --> 02:04:10,692
I mean, that leaves no room for anything.

1435
02:04:10,752 --> 02:04:13,233
It's basically here you go, accept it or nothing.

1436
02:04:13,873 --> 02:04:14,953
That's what the 28th means.

1437
02:04:15,333 --> 02:04:26,196
So again, you know, we've, we've scheduled, we've, we've raised this issue as councilor, as president Morrell just said for months.

1438
02:04:28,119 --> 02:04:29,639
The timeline obviously changed.

1439
02:04:29,679 --> 02:04:34,141
Obviously, I'm sure there are explanations and reasons for that, or at least some sort of statement to the effect of it.

1440
02:04:34,301 --> 02:04:48,705
But while I would be happy to try to provide the information and bring it around to my fellow councillors, you know, and do that, because I want people to have as much information as they can have as soon before the meeting as they can have it, doesn't mean that I think this is the right way to do this.

1441
02:04:51,387 --> 02:05:01,995
You know, as one person who got a budget book and read the whole budget book and had posted notes on every page and a note on every page and looking through the narrative and goals and why asked about those things tonight which we don't have.

1442
02:05:03,776 --> 02:05:10,280
That would make me, you know, that's what my vision of a budget process is.

1443
02:05:10,701 --> 02:05:16,044
This is what we, the best we can do with the limited things that we've been given.

1444
02:05:16,144 --> 02:05:20,527
So just to also basically make the same point that President Morrell made.

1445
02:05:20,747 --> 02:05:23,069
And on that, what's gonna happen is, right?

1446
02:05:23,209 --> 02:05:28,853
If the budget doesn't pass and the administration has to make the hard decisions that we asked them to make three fiscal years ago, you know what they're gonna say?

1447
02:05:28,873 --> 02:05:30,214
Well, the council didn't pass the budget.

1448
02:05:30,754 --> 02:05:31,815
Well, the council didn't do it.

1449
02:05:32,175 --> 02:05:33,256
Well, the council didn't do it.

1450
02:05:33,276 --> 02:05:34,116
It's the council's fault.

1451
02:05:34,356 --> 02:05:36,617
We've asked for these decisions to be made three years ago.

1452
02:05:36,937 --> 02:05:43,380
Three fiscal years ago, three budgets ago, we've been asking for the reliance on one-time revenues to be, to move away from that.

1453
02:05:43,660 --> 02:05:44,880
Three years we've been asking for it.

1454
02:05:45,301 --> 02:05:48,202
And then at the end of the day, it's going to be, it's the council's fault because they didn't approve the budget.

1455
02:05:49,622 --> 02:05:53,244
The council right now is acting in a way that's fiscally responsible and adult.

1456
02:05:53,884 --> 02:05:57,406
And the reason that we're doing it is because we don't want to mortgage the financial future of this community.

1457
02:06:01,789 --> 02:06:18,303
Thank you President Morrell and of course I have no interest in being redundant or piling on but just speaking from my personal experience of a first time counselor I think part of my frustration is I really do my best because I feel it's my responsibility to people that put me in office to come prepared to every meeting.

1458
02:06:18,423 --> 02:06:19,844
This is my first budget season.

1459
02:06:20,945 --> 02:06:21,666
The homework is real.

1460
02:06:22,266 --> 02:06:25,789
And so that's why it's not only frustrating but distressing to know that.

1461
02:06:26,470 --> 02:06:34,673
There might be extremely limited time to come to a budget hearing to vote on the operating budget for the next fiscal year I know this is an immense responsibility I take it extremely seriously.

1462
02:06:34,693 --> 02:06:43,457
And that's why it's so it holds so much weight for me, the way that this process is being conducted and I fully understand nobody in this building is happy about it.

1463
02:06:44,077 --> 02:06:47,278
But I do want to go on the record in invoicing that.

1464
02:06:47,299 --> 02:06:57,803
And I think that's why it's also compoundingly frustrating to reflect on what we're asking for in this budget is to be empowered to do what this body does in our system of government, which is to legislate.

1465
02:06:58,663 --> 02:07:04,426
It's hard to feel like we're being empowered to make responsible, deliberate decisions about the budget.

1466
02:07:04,526 --> 02:07:06,667
It's hard to feel like we're being empowered to make

1467
02:07:07,647 --> 02:07:13,413
deliberate legislation, when a lot of the budget priorities we have asked for.

1468
02:07:15,075 --> 02:07:23,343
We are not able to discuss, let alone see considered so I just want to put that out there for the record, I want this body to be empowered to do its job.

1469
02:07:23,643 --> 02:07:23,944
Thank you.

1470
02:07:25,305 --> 02:07:30,390
Madam President also underneath this process when you look at it right, you look at the council's power and authority we can add to the budget.

1471
02:07:31,460 --> 02:07:35,904
But we can reduce the budget and we can also do line item vetoes and move money around, right?

1472
02:07:36,044 --> 02:07:41,648
So when we have a budget like this and we say the executive has $1.19 million in their budget, we're looking for 50.

1473
02:07:43,049 --> 02:07:51,496
We don't know what line item, we can even say reduce legislative line item, an increase, reduce executive line item and increase legislative line item.

1474
02:07:51,536 --> 02:07:52,257
We can't even do that.

1475
02:07:53,238 --> 02:07:54,579
We can't even perform those functions.

1476
02:07:58,118 --> 02:08:09,885
I think, you know, to everyone's point, regardless of who is sitting in these seven seats, no one can operate at the level that this city deserves with this forced urgency and lack of clarity.

1477
02:08:10,746 --> 02:08:11,686
And that's what we're left with.

1478
02:08:12,607 --> 02:08:13,608
So I just want to make that point.

1479
02:08:14,408 --> 02:08:16,069
Chief of Staff Nazarian, you had your hand up.

1480
02:08:18,491 --> 02:08:18,851
Thank you.

1481
02:08:20,012 --> 02:08:23,634
I just wanted to address a couple of comments that were made in particular.

1482
02:08:23,654 --> 02:08:24,595
I think that the

1483
02:08:25,331 --> 02:08:30,975
point in which I began speaking, I was, I believe Councilor Knight had a point of information.

1484
02:08:31,496 --> 02:08:33,317
That's when a number of assumptions were stated.

1485
02:08:33,897 --> 02:08:35,639
And I want to clear the record on that.

1486
02:08:36,079 --> 02:08:43,064
The first is that one assumption that was stated and appears to have taken away is that these budgets are not ready.

1487
02:08:43,384 --> 02:08:44,505
That's an inaccurate statement.

1488
02:08:45,278 --> 02:08:46,219
They're not before us.

1489
02:08:46,759 --> 02:08:49,982
Allow me to explain, please allow me the opportunity to explain.

1490
02:08:50,002 --> 02:08:56,367
I do I over the course of the last two evenings I've been before you and I've had multiple interruptions.

1491
02:08:56,407 --> 02:08:58,889
I have not been able to explain things at times.

1492
02:08:59,549 --> 02:09:02,131
So please allow me the opportunity to explain and I will do that.

1493
02:09:03,832 --> 02:09:09,897
As stated in the documentation that was provided to the city council yesterday evening, there were proposed budgets.

1494
02:09:10,505 --> 02:09:21,876
that were proposed by our departments, as a result of the difficulties that we faced with the revenue information, we've begun to scrub the numbers, and that is why there are modifications being made to these budgets.

1495
02:09:22,236 --> 02:09:24,118
So just want to set the record straight on that.

1496
02:09:25,302 --> 02:09:32,243
Furthermore, there are lines that we're adding to these documents in lieu of the fact that you don't have the budget book before you.

1497
02:09:32,643 --> 02:09:42,605
And that is to make sure that you have the full-time equivalents and those tables below so that you have, you know, the basic foundation of the documents that you would need to ask questions.

1498
02:09:43,185 --> 02:09:50,747
Obviously, there's other pieces to the budget book that wouldn't be there, but the narrative or obviously like the organizational chart.

1499
02:09:50,767 --> 02:09:51,887
I think that's by and large,

1500
02:09:52,627 --> 02:09:54,008
the pieces that are remaining.

1501
02:09:54,628 --> 02:10:02,910
So I want to make that clear that these are just we want to make sure when we give you documentation, we're giving you accurate information, and we're not doing multiple revisions.

1502
02:10:03,811 --> 02:10:07,452
Again, that's just I just wanted to make those points clear.

1503
02:10:08,352 --> 02:10:08,672
Thank you.

1504
02:10:09,633 --> 02:10:16,335
And I do just want to know as you know, historically, or you know, two years I've been on the council or any city anywhere.

1505
02:10:16,996 --> 02:10:26,362
You know the budget is submitted on the regular agenda it's you know it has this piece of paper we were given last night it's officially submitted, then we have the committees of the whole so we have that information.

1506
02:10:26,862 --> 02:10:35,807
we're working backwards, because we have no choice and I and I understand what you're saying, but I feel like we're just playing with semantics at this point, and this is nothing against you personally.

1507
02:10:36,308 --> 02:10:40,330
You know, this is, this is a full contact sport here, unfortunately, because we're fighting

1508
02:10:40,989 --> 02:10:41,729
for our constituents.

1509
02:10:41,769 --> 02:10:43,930
We're fighting for the phone calls we get all the time.

1510
02:10:43,990 --> 02:10:44,710
We can hide.

1511
02:10:45,330 --> 02:10:46,491
We're here every Tuesday night.

1512
02:10:47,111 --> 02:10:47,911
People can see us.

1513
02:10:47,971 --> 02:10:49,212
They can come to us.

1514
02:10:50,192 --> 02:10:51,633
And that's where the frustration comes from.

1515
02:10:52,193 --> 02:10:56,494
And just the frustration that we're not being put in a position to do our jobs to the best of the ability.

1516
02:10:59,615 --> 02:11:04,197
We could go on and on, but I mean, this is where we are.

1517
02:11:05,522 --> 02:11:13,944
And I respect that, and we're doing our best to do everything we possibly can at this point in time to get as much information accurately as possible to the City Council.

1518
02:11:14,364 --> 02:11:20,206
This was not anticipated, especially given the changes in the ARPA revenue loss calculation.

1519
02:11:21,766 --> 02:11:26,428
We went over it yesterday, and I don't want to take up the City Council's time to go over it again today.

1520
02:11:26,908 --> 02:11:29,369
This is the first time we're dealing with $48 million.

1521
02:11:29,449 --> 02:11:31,449
This is the first time we're dealing with a pandemic.

1522
02:11:31,949 --> 02:11:34,590
This is the first time we've gone through these issues.

1523
02:11:36,238 --> 02:11:36,918
So thank you.

1524
02:11:37,899 --> 02:11:40,741
I mean, honestly, sorry, Madam President.

1525
02:11:42,322 --> 02:11:44,563
Fundamentally, you can say it however you want to say it.

1526
02:11:45,084 --> 02:11:46,805
There's been no budget proposed to this council.

1527
02:11:46,925 --> 02:11:53,809
So functionally we're holding these hearings to help you reach the end goal of passing a budget before June 30th.

1528
02:11:54,850 --> 02:11:56,491
You put a proposed a budget on the 28th.

1529
02:11:57,231 --> 02:11:58,512
Are we having budget hearings in July?

1530
02:11:59,792 --> 02:12:02,493
That's how it would have worked if we waited for this budget to be submitted.

1531
02:12:03,093 --> 02:12:04,793
And we do not have a comprehensive look.

1532
02:12:05,453 --> 02:12:14,035
I'm really glad that we asked last Friday when we heard about the urgent crisis, we said, here's the key information that we think we need by Tuesday to start the process, to have the top lines.

1533
02:12:14,075 --> 02:12:19,337
And I'm glad it was provided because it at least lets us get going on this in some form or fashion.

1534
02:12:19,797 --> 02:12:26,718
But there, you can say that when we say the budgets aren't complete, the budgets aren't complete, but we do not have a budget book in front of us.

1535
02:12:26,798 --> 02:12:28,299
There's no comprehensive view of the budget.

1536
02:12:28,319 --> 02:12:29,359
There's no budget before us.

1537
02:12:30,199 --> 02:12:35,861
And quite frankly, you know, this whole, we just found out about ARPA yesterday.

1538
02:12:35,881 --> 02:12:38,462
We didn't have the calculation for months.

1539
02:12:38,522 --> 02:12:40,222
We were waiting to get the calculation for months.

1540
02:12:40,282 --> 02:12:44,764
We should not have made budget assumptions based on a calculation and a number that we didn't have.

1541
02:12:45,204 --> 02:12:47,345
That's not the fault of this council.

1542
02:12:47,445 --> 02:12:49,265
It's not, we just found out last week.

1543
02:12:49,425 --> 02:12:51,026
It's your budget assumptions.

1544
02:12:51,506 --> 02:12:54,527
We're assuming that we would have money that we found out we didn't have.

1545
02:12:55,466 --> 02:13:05,210
Now sure we do that in some ways, the cherry sheet is an assumption assuming they're going to pass the budget, any even in a sense prop two and a half is assumption assuming that new growth and revenue grows that way I understand that.

1546
02:13:05,671 --> 02:13:10,813
But when it comes to specific one time revenue specific things like you know that the ARPA rules.

1547
02:13:12,540 --> 02:13:16,281
That's something months ago that shouldn't have been assumed into a budget.

1548
02:13:16,741 --> 02:13:23,063
So you shouldn't be changing at the last minute every number and scaling everything down, and that's not our fault.

1549
02:13:23,463 --> 02:13:24,843
It's nothing we can do about that.

1550
02:13:24,883 --> 02:13:30,484
That's an assumption that was made on in the administration months ago to say, we expect we're going to have this number.

1551
02:13:31,265 --> 02:13:32,285
And, you know,

1552
02:13:33,533 --> 02:13:44,556
That just shouldn't have been the way that it was operated because clearly it's created this situation where, I mean, I can't even begin to tell you what people think this is.

1553
02:13:44,817 --> 02:13:48,558
I do have some trust that you got the calculation last week and that's why it is.

1554
02:13:49,138 --> 02:13:56,620
You don't even wanna know the number of people who are coming to me and saying, oh, this has gotta be a last minute play about union contracts or the school budget or a million other things.

1555
02:13:56,700 --> 02:13:57,541
It looks horrible.

1556
02:13:57,961 --> 02:13:59,721
It's just not the way the budgeting should be done.

1557
02:13:59,781 --> 02:14:01,402
It's not the way the process should be done.

1558
02:14:02,542 --> 02:14:07,266
So, again, as Councilor, as President Morrell said, it's not personal.

1559
02:14:07,826 --> 02:14:25,078
I understand you're both working really hard, but someone at some point, and my guess is with under this system of government it's really only one person at some point the mayor said, assume we're going to have 8 million in ARPA and make the budget on that even though we're not going to have the calculation until the books are complete, and we actually have the information to make that calculation.

1560
02:14:25,878 --> 02:14:31,880
And I'm sorry that that may have put you guys in the position of scrambling to get a budget before us, but it doesn't change the timeline.

1561
02:14:31,920 --> 02:14:35,261
It doesn't change state statute and it doesn't change the fact that's why we're all sitting here.

1562
02:14:35,961 --> 02:14:42,363
Quite frankly, I think being nicer than we want to be compared to the amount of fury that a lot of us have that we're in this position.

1563
02:14:43,223 --> 02:14:48,044
So again, it's not, it's not about you as a person.

1564
02:14:48,544 --> 02:14:50,985
We've had great meetings and work together on a lot of things.

1565
02:14:51,385 --> 02:14:52,125
It's not about that.

1566
02:14:52,145 --> 02:14:54,066
I don't think you're working really hard to get us what we need.

1567
02:14:54,722 --> 02:14:56,984
but someone at some point made a decision to put us here.

1568
02:14:57,064 --> 02:15:00,887
And if there's not going to be accountability for that, it's going to get worse before it gets better.

1569
02:15:00,907 --> 02:15:04,689
Thank you, Madam President.

1570
02:15:04,890 --> 02:15:11,995
And I know yesterday, my emotions really, I won't, I won't even say get the best of me because that was my emotions.

1571
02:15:12,035 --> 02:15:12,876
That's how I'm feeling.

1572
02:15:13,837 --> 02:15:34,569
for the fact that I have been answering phone calls, for the fact that I feel like I am just so unprepared for the first time I feel in my life as an elected official with eight years in the school committee and eight years in the council, that I'm not prepared to give anyone the answer they deserve.

1573
02:15:34,729 --> 02:15:41,973
And sometimes, sometimes as adults, you should look yourself in the mirror and just own it.

1574
02:15:43,757 --> 02:15:51,160
don't come up to a podium and give excuses where the Commonwealth has gone through this.

1575
02:15:52,261 --> 02:15:53,901
Neighbor communities have gone through this.

1576
02:15:55,762 --> 02:16:03,706
Maybe what's frustrating, I worked for municipality that I was part of the pre-budgeting process.

1577
02:16:04,226 --> 02:16:05,967
I went through the process.

1578
02:16:07,365 --> 02:16:09,146
We expressed our interest.

1579
02:16:09,847 --> 02:16:16,212
We worked with our opera coordinators, making sure that we work with the city administration to get what we need.

1580
02:16:18,954 --> 02:16:22,857
And even if there were surprises, they were prepared for that.

1581
02:16:24,678 --> 02:16:26,780
There was different percentages.

1582
02:16:28,027 --> 02:16:38,090
wishlist from the beginning, department heads, wishlist with the level fund budget, with an adding of 10%, an adding of 20%, a minus of 10%.

1583
02:16:38,710 --> 02:16:41,070
This is how you prepare that budget.

1584
02:16:43,251 --> 02:16:45,692
Now we could say, well, we didn't have a budget director.

1585
02:16:46,052 --> 02:16:47,312
We didn't have a finance director.

1586
02:16:47,692 --> 02:16:50,233
I understand this isn't Mr. Dixon's issue right now.

1587
02:16:51,527 --> 02:16:58,132
But we have talked to nauseam about consultants at every different level in this community.

1588
02:17:00,193 --> 02:17:04,296
And the most important one for us is the budget.

1589
02:17:06,978 --> 02:17:17,006
So I'm not going to get heated, I'm not going to get angry, but please, sometimes it's just better to stand up and own it.

1590
02:17:19,000 --> 02:17:27,927
And I apologize that the chief of staff has to be the person that has to come up and present this because I know it doesn't fall on one person.

1591
02:17:29,729 --> 02:17:39,117
But I will tell you my frustration is that I truly thought that we would share in successes and share in failures.

1592
02:17:39,757 --> 02:17:43,400
That's what discussion I've had with you and I don't see it.

1593
02:17:44,641 --> 02:17:45,762
So to come up and say,

1594
02:17:46,830 --> 02:17:54,132
that it's this, this, and this, instead of saying, we weren't prepared, let's move forward.

1595
02:17:54,692 --> 02:18:04,715
That would go a lot, it would hold more weight with the people I've talked to, and especially the way I feel, because this is frustrating.

1596
02:18:05,535 --> 02:18:05,835
This is,

1597
02:18:08,545 --> 02:18:20,581
For someone who loves this city and lives in the city and grew up in the city and lives with my neighbors and have to listen to everybody every single day on how this hurts them.

1598
02:18:21,555 --> 02:18:40,989
and the possibility of my neighbors moving because they need to feel that they need to move to a better community, or teachers that I've worked with, or principals that I've worked with, or mentored me that are moving on because they don't feel that it's worth it here.

1599
02:18:41,290 --> 02:18:45,112
And knowing that the children in our community are gonna lose those valuable people.

1600
02:18:46,994 --> 02:18:48,315
To me, this is what's hurting.

1601
02:18:49,723 --> 02:18:57,487
And maybe the city administration should understand, this is a huge part, at least for me, I'm hurting.

1602
02:18:59,208 --> 02:19:07,132
So if I made someone feel uncomfortable in any way, or I was too abrupt, well, you know what?

1603
02:19:07,772 --> 02:19:10,534
That's my personality in the sense that we're hurting here.

1604
02:19:12,294 --> 02:19:13,235
And instead of saying,

1605
02:19:13,803 --> 02:19:15,823
We own it, let's move forward and fix it.

1606
02:19:16,344 --> 02:19:18,544
We're saying, let's blame all this.

1607
02:19:19,444 --> 02:19:24,626
I didn't say a word in tonight's budget, this presentation, because it's not a presentation.

1608
02:19:24,966 --> 02:19:33,368
All due respect, it's a numbers that, as I pull out last year's book, I see those numbers and I just mirror it today.

1609
02:19:35,708 --> 02:19:37,589
And that's it, it's just frustrating.

1610
02:19:39,009 --> 02:19:43,030
And if frustrating is something bad, I'll own that.

1611
02:19:44,223 --> 02:19:45,124
because I'm frustrated.

1612
02:19:46,345 --> 02:19:47,606
So I apologize.

1613
02:19:47,826 --> 02:20:02,897
And as we move forward, I know I cannot, I'm going to stay, I can say today, if we really get this book a few days ahead of time, there is no way as a counselor that, that,

1614
02:20:03,520 --> 02:20:15,965
takes a lot of ownership, as Councilor Collins mentioned, to study and understand and talk to department heads and work together with them and understand what the issues are and the concerns are with our community.

1615
02:20:16,305 --> 02:20:25,649
And knowing that you can have everything and understanding that, but not even having that opportunity, how can we even consider taking a vote?

1616
02:20:26,109 --> 02:20:27,750
I just don't, I just can't see it.

1617
02:20:28,928 --> 02:20:29,488
We have nothing.

1618
02:20:29,508 --> 02:20:30,689
Our number one priority is what?

1619
02:20:31,330 --> 02:20:32,891
What is our number one priority here in the council?

1620
02:20:33,271 --> 02:20:34,532
Everybody wants to know what it is.

1621
02:20:35,493 --> 02:20:36,634
And you have power to do what?

1622
02:20:36,714 --> 02:20:37,695
Everybody keeps telling me.

1623
02:20:38,155 --> 02:20:39,336
What power do we have, everyone?

1624
02:20:39,876 --> 02:20:42,078
We have the budget and ordinances.

1625
02:20:44,019 --> 02:20:44,860
Budget's number one.

1626
02:20:47,022 --> 02:20:48,923
And there is no budget book.

1627
02:20:49,463 --> 02:20:57,950
There is no presentation because the way it was presented, the way it was put together, wasn't put together with the forethought of

1628
02:20:59,880 --> 02:21:04,763
an $8 million shortfall or an $8 million increase.

1629
02:21:05,263 --> 02:21:06,224
It was right down the middle.

1630
02:21:07,485 --> 02:21:09,346
And this is a wishlist because that's not a budget.

1631
02:21:09,826 --> 02:21:10,627
That's a wishlist.

1632
02:21:12,168 --> 02:21:14,669
And I like, again, I said, it's frustrating.

1633
02:21:15,010 --> 02:21:22,394
Maybe I should leave my municipality job because it's frustrating to see how that process works and what we do here.

1634
02:21:22,414 --> 02:21:27,097
So I know people don't like when I make this comparison,

1635
02:21:30,346 --> 02:21:31,046
It is what it is.

1636
02:21:31,066 --> 02:21:33,387
So thank you, Madam President.

1637
02:21:33,407 --> 02:21:33,967
I apologize.

1638
02:21:36,128 --> 02:21:37,028
Thank you, Mr. Tavarelli.

1639
02:21:37,048 --> 02:21:46,871
Before we adjourn, I just want to note that this first Saturday is scheduled fire, Department of Public Works, buildings, facilities, finance, information technology, and veterans.

1640
02:21:46,951 --> 02:21:49,111
And that meeting notice is posted, I believe.

1641
02:21:50,031 --> 02:21:51,392
If it's not live yet, it will be live.

1642
02:21:51,512 --> 02:21:53,072
It has to be live by tomorrow morning.

1643
02:21:54,833 --> 02:21:55,533
And then I'll let you adjourn.

1644
02:21:58,501 --> 02:22:01,783
If I may quickly, I don't know that I really will be quick.

1645
02:22:02,264 --> 02:22:03,725
I don't know that this is going to add value.

1646
02:22:04,545 --> 02:22:15,692
But I want to say one thing very quickly first, which is I appreciate the discussion this evening and the way that the discussion was presented this evening and the topics.

1647
02:22:16,253 --> 02:22:21,936
Yesterday evening, I feel very differently about the way that comments were made and statements were made.

1648
02:22:23,208 --> 02:22:24,408
I'd just like to delineate that.

1649
02:22:24,609 --> 02:22:30,751
And I'd like to say, I know that things can get heated sometimes, but there is a line and that's that.

1650
02:22:31,751 --> 02:22:36,433
Now, moving to the real material point that I wanted to make.

1651
02:22:36,793 --> 02:22:46,157
As chief of staff, I am responsible and I'm not going to, I don't know how much value that adds here right now at this time, based on all the frustrations.

1652
02:22:46,797 --> 02:22:47,697
Sounds like I'm late.

1653
02:22:48,318 --> 02:22:51,459
I am responsible for this timing.

1654
02:22:53,252 --> 02:23:10,250
I'm not going to stand before you and tell you that we hired consultants, that we hired an interim finance director, that we hired different staff, because I don't think that that adds value to this process, that we did try everything we could to get to a better place than we are today.

1655
02:23:10,971 --> 02:23:14,455
But I do wanna just say that I do take responsibility.

1656
02:23:15,155 --> 02:23:17,397
I am very sorry that we're where we are right now.

1657
02:23:17,758 --> 02:23:20,180
I don't want any of you to be in this position.

1658
02:23:20,280 --> 02:23:24,024
And as you can imagine, I don't enjoy being in the position that I'm in right now.

1659
02:23:25,025 --> 02:23:25,325
Thank you.

1660
02:23:32,078 --> 02:23:35,340
I'm confused here, because it's not about anybody in this room.

1661
02:23:35,780 --> 02:23:39,042
It's about this community in this city, and what's fair to them and what's right to them.

1662
02:23:39,422 --> 02:23:45,005
We're only frustrated because it's not right, and it's not fair to the taxpayers and the people who live in this community.

1663
02:23:45,666 --> 02:23:46,666
That's why we're mad.

1664
02:23:47,326 --> 02:23:47,707
We're mad.

1665
02:23:47,727 --> 02:23:49,868
I mean, if you want to take ownership of it, then take ownership of it.

1666
02:23:49,888 --> 02:23:51,129
If it's your fault, that's great.

1667
02:23:51,169 --> 02:23:55,531
So that's why we haven't had quarterly meetings looking at revenue forecasts and revenue projections.

1668
02:23:55,551 --> 02:23:57,112
And that's why we haven't gotten the Warren articles.

1669
02:23:58,583 --> 02:24:02,244
If that's what it is, if that's where the blame's to go, that's where the blame's to go, all right?

1670
02:24:02,264 --> 02:24:03,785
But we're gonna have to get past that, right?

1671
02:24:03,805 --> 02:24:06,345
We're gonna have to move forward one way or another, right?

1672
02:24:06,385 --> 02:24:07,426
Councilor Beasley's right on that.

1673
02:24:07,606 --> 02:24:09,006
We're gonna have to move forward one way or another.

1674
02:24:09,326 --> 02:24:16,189
But it's not about us being angry, it's about this community and what we feel as though the community's getting, and they're getting less than they deserve.

1675
02:24:16,789 --> 02:24:17,949
And that's really where we're coming from.

1676
02:24:18,029 --> 02:24:26,392
And the process is just an absolute reflection of the amount of respect that you give us, and in turn, the members of this community that put us here to make these decisions.

1677
02:24:26,932 --> 02:24:28,533
So that's where the frustration lies.

1678
02:24:30,034 --> 02:24:32,797
And the other thing is, how many bosses do you have?

1679
02:24:32,837 --> 02:24:33,737
You only have one boss.

1680
02:24:34,458 --> 02:24:35,238
You answer to the mayor.

1681
02:24:36,299 --> 02:24:38,521
We answer to the 60,000 residents in this community.

1682
02:24:39,402 --> 02:24:46,047
And then most of the department heads in this community come 4.30, get in their car, and they drive down the bumpy streets.

1683
02:24:46,487 --> 02:24:50,190
And then it says entering whatever town it is, and the streets get smooth, and they go home.

1684
02:24:51,131 --> 02:24:53,873
But I go to the supermarket, and I go to Domet's for donuts.

1685
02:24:55,573 --> 02:24:57,814
I go to the park for my kids game and I got to listen to it.

1686
02:24:58,375 --> 02:25:04,679
I'm not hiding down the Cape and how much I'm here in the community listening to it.

1687
02:25:05,859 --> 02:25:10,843
So if I got to listen to it, the man should have listened to it too, because that's what I'm here for.

1688
02:25:11,083 --> 02:25:14,645
I'm here to express and represent the interest of these individuals in this community.

1689
02:25:14,925 --> 02:25:16,106
It's not about me, it's about them.

1690
02:25:16,886 --> 02:25:20,008
I want that to be very clear.

1691
02:25:20,268 --> 02:25:21,009
Yep.

1692
02:25:21,229 --> 02:25:24,051
And I'm just going to add this cause I, I want to get out of here too.

1693
02:25:25,480 --> 02:25:29,584
If we're going to delineate between last night and tonight, tonight was not substantive.

1694
02:25:29,684 --> 02:25:30,745
Last night was substantive.

1695
02:25:31,225 --> 02:25:33,507
That's the delineation I have between last night and tonight.

1696
02:25:33,847 --> 02:25:38,611
I understand there was uncomfortability last night with certain elements or whatever.

1697
02:25:38,631 --> 02:25:39,973
I mean, nothing has been specified.

1698
02:25:40,413 --> 02:25:45,117
Last night was a substantive discussion about the basic top line overviews of revenue expenses in the budget of the city.

1699
02:25:45,457 --> 02:25:50,842
And it was an incredibly difficult conversation because we're in an incredibly difficult position with an incredibly difficult timeline.

1700
02:25:51,533 --> 02:25:57,098
So tonight felt good because it was mostly, honestly, nice questions that had no budget impact.

1701
02:25:57,558 --> 02:25:59,100
That's why tonight felt better than last night.

1702
02:25:59,861 --> 02:26:06,386
The more substantive budget discussions we're gonna have, I'm sure the more uncomfortability that a lot of people, including me, are gonna feel.

1703
02:26:08,508 --> 02:26:14,033
So on the motion of Councilor Knight to adjourn, seconded by Vice President Behrs.

1704
02:26:14,233 --> 02:26:15,014
All those in favor?

1705
02:26:15,034 --> 02:26:16,495
All those opposed?

1706
02:26:17,156 --> 02:26:17,757
Meeting is adjourned.

